Categories:
- liked: User expressed positive sentiment (enjoyed, loved, great, interesting, amazing, fan of, etc.)
- disliked: User expressed negative or lukewarm sentiment (didn't like, hated, boring, mediocre, okay, decent, not great, etc.)
- not_seen: User explicitly said they haven't seen/watched it ("haven't seen", "no", "not yet", "never watched")

IMPORTANT RULES:
- DO NOT drop any movies as "neutral" - everything goes to liked, disliked, or not_seen
- "okay" / "decent" / "alright" / "not bad" → DISLIKED (lukewarm = not liked)
- "Haven't seen that" / "No" / "Not yet" → MUST go to "not_seen"
- Only include entities explicitly mentioned by the user
- Use exact names from conversation
- Return valid JSON only, no explanations

Examples:
- "I enjoy sci-fi" → liked: ["sci-fi"]
- "Loved that movie!" → liked: [the movie]
- "It was okay I guess" → disliked: [the movie]
- "Meh, not my thing" → disliked: [the movie]
- "Horror isn't really my thing" → disliked: ["horror"]
- "Haven't seen that one" → not_seen: [the movie being discussed]

